.idea/
.claude/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
ios/VerifierLabApp/VerifierLabApp.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/
# xcshareddata is ignored except for xcschemes, which has to be tracked: a
# shared scheme is how `xcodebuild -scheme` finds the target, and without one
# in the checkout build-ios fails on CI while succeeding locally, because
# Xcode autocreates a private copy under the ignored xcuserdata. The glob is
# `/*` rather than `/` so git descends into the directory -- a trailing-slash
# exclude cannot be undone by a later negation.
# Tracking it means Xcode writes into a tracked file: editing scheme
# environment variables in the UI bakes the developer's own host into the
# scheme, and `QRTRUST_VERIFIER_BASE_URLS` there beats the generated
# LocalProvider.xcconfig (ProcessInfo wins over the bundle value in
# VerifierAPI). Put machine-specific endpoints in the ignored
# LocalProvider.xcconfig via scripts/write_ios_local_provider_config.sh and
# keep the scheme free of them; only the maintainer `make release-audit`
# catches a leak here, never CI (see release/public_release_checklist.md §6e).
ios/VerifierLabApp/VerifierLabApp.xcodeproj/xcshareddata/*
!ios/VerifierLabApp/VerifierLabApp.xcodeproj/xcshareddata/xcschemes/

